2026-07-27T08:49:30.7450329Z duckdb keeps downloaded extensions and secrets in a temporary directory:
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7451047Z i /tmp/RtmpWe40OP/duckdb
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7451420Z This is removed when the R session ends.
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7451855Z * Extensions are re-downloaded each session.
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7452477Z * Secrets are lost.
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7453368Z i Run duckdb(shared_home = TRUE) (or create ~/.duckdb) to keep them (suitable for most users).
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7454247Z i Run duckdb(shared_home = FALSE) to accept the temporary directory (and silence this message).
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7454865Z i See ?duckdb_storage for details and alternatives.
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7689961Z   'test-storage-message-once.R:52:3' [success]
2026-07-27T08:49:30.7795762Z   'test-storage-message-once.R:53:3' [success]
2026-07-27T08:49:30.8210112Z   'test-storage-message-once.R:59:3' [success]
2026-07-27T08:49:30.8356224Z End test: reusing a cached on-disk driver does not record a storage choice
